From 1df996420832a35fbde9c92a80661b44d0380a25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 01:27:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Show the globe of a MarbleWidget in stereo 3D on Wayland

The globe is drawn once for each eye into two views the size of the
widget, which a wl_subsurface under the window's surface shows side by
side, left eye first, declared once as full side by side stereo content.
The widget is a transparent hole over it, where the interface layers are
painted once, so they stay on the screen plane in both eyes.

setStereo3D() is off by default and has effect where the compositor
takes stereo content (isStereo3DSupported(), Wayland only: not on xcb)
and the window was prepared with prepareStereo3DWindow(). Built when
stereo-declare, Wayland and Qt's private GUI headers are found.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
